Subject: fix: include format_element.h for FormatElement completeness

language.cc calls empty() on the std::vector<FormatElement> returned by
Rule::GetLatinFormat(), but rule.h only forward-declares FormatElement.
libc++ now implements vector::empty() as size() == 0, which performs
pointer arithmetic that requires a complete element type under the
pointer-based (stable ABI) vector layout Electron builds with.

